  "about": "With over 25 years of experience at the hardware-software boundary, I architect the firmware foundations that power global cloud infrastructure and high-performance computing (HPC) clusters. My expertise lies in EDK2/UEFI development for complex, multi-socket platforms, with a relentless focus on platform security, RAS, and high-speed interconnect optimization.\n\nThroughout my career at Oracle Corporation and Sun Microsystems, I have bridged the gap between silicon design and system deployment. I’ve led global engineering teams through massive technical shifts—from x86 to ARM and from legacy SVN to modern Git-based CI/CD—ensuring that firmware is never the bottleneck for innovation.\n\nCore Expertise:\n\tSystem Architecture: Multi-socket server bring-up, PCIe bifurcation, and GPU interconnect tuning.\n\tPlatform Security: Root of Trust (RoT), CRTM, and secure boot compliance for hyperscale environments.\n\tTechnical Leadership: Orchestrating cross-functional strategies between silicon, hardware, and OS teams to maximize system-level performance.\n\nI am passionate about tackling the industry’s most difficult firmware problems and mentoring the next generation of engineers who build the world’s most powerful systems.",
